" role="menuitemradio" tabindex="-1"><div class="aBBjbd MbhUzd" jsname="ksKsZd"></div><div class="uyYuVb oJeWuf" jscontroller="cCHjWd" jsaction="JIbuQc:Hw9KTb" jsname="Hw9KTb" jslog="77040; 1:1214; track:click;"><div class="O7wNO"></div><div class="jO7h3c">Spam</div></div></span><span jsslot="" class="z80M1" jsaction="click:o6ZaF(preventDefault=true); mousedown:lAhnzb; mouseup:Osgxgf; mouseenter:SKyDAe; mouseleave:xq3APb;touchstart:jJiBRc; touchmove:kZeBdd; touchend:VfAz8(preventMouseEvents=true)" jsname="j7LFlb" aria-label="Link to this review" role="menuitem" tabindex="-1"><div class="aBBjbd MbhUzd" jsname="ksKsZd"></div><div class="uyYuVb oJeWuf" jscontroller="cCHjWd" jsaction="JIbuQc:kuHRr" jsname="kuHRr" jslog="77039; 1:6066; track:click;"><div class="jO7h3c">Link to this review</div></div></span></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div jscontroller="LVJlx" class="UD7Dzf"> <span jsname="bN97Pc">I really like what this app does, but there are a couple of things that either it's missing or that I just can't find that would make it perfect. 1. I really, REALLY want to be able to lock the dimensions of rooms and objects once I've input them. It's infuriating to accidentally resize the room whe...<div class="cQj82c"><button class="LkLjZd ScJHi OzU4dc  " jsaction="click:TiglPc" jsname="gxjVle">Full Review</button></div></span><span jsname="fbQN7e" style="display: none;">I really like what this app does, but there are a couple of things that either it's missing or that I just can't find that would make it perfect. 1. I really, REALLY want to be able to lock the dimensions of rooms and objects once I've input them. It's infuriating to accidentally resize the room when I'm trying to select and move an object away from the wall! This is the most important function to me that I can't figure out. If anyone knows how to make it happen, PLEASE let me know ASAP! 2. I would love to be able to enter dimensions of my furniture so that I don't have to reenter things, and have them be labelled (for example, I have a bunch of Hemnes glass door cabinets from IKEA. I'd like to be able to create them as preexisting furnishings that I could pull automatically from the right hand menu). 3. I wish that I could name pieces of furniture on my floor plan (ex, "dresser" or "Electric Fireplace Cabinet"). Otherwise, I lose track of what I'm looking at. 4. I wish that I could mark the locations of outlet switches and HVAC vents so that I don't accidentally plan to put furniture directly over a floor vent. If any of these functions exist and I've missed how to make them work, please let me know how! Otherwise, I'd love to see the developer add these things.</span></div><div class="LVQB0b"><div class="QoPmEb"></div><div><span class="X43Kjb">Marcin Lewandowski</span><span class="p2TkOb">October 1, 2018</span></div>1. Tap interior edge of a wall to select it and then you can use lock icons in the toolbar to lock its length and position. The same for symbols and doors.
2. I have this (user library) nearly ready and I hope to release it in a few weeks.
3. Use labels from Annotations tab.
4. There are switches under Electric category or you could use labels too.</div></div></div></div><div jscontroller="H6eOGe" jsmodel="y8Aajc" jsdata="yf3HXc;gp:AOqpTOHjGF1t_i2RBF1pBsqhU-XvjqCSstVwQ9OO6aDaLaADokFqwDAI2G8mBoeAQfQWEqK-XTjf1pP84QOvHA;$884 YjFXEf;_;$256"><div class="zc7KVe"><div class="vDSMeb bAhLNe" aria-hidden="true"><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-bQU5WqhB9U4/AAAAAAAAAAI/AAAAAAAAAAA/AMZuucmbz-ClJiC07aEu95fO-fIrTYB4cg/w48-h48-n/photo.jpg" srcset="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-bQU5WqhB9U4/AAAAAAAAAAI/AAAAAAAAAAA/AMZuucmbz-ClJiC07aEu95fO-fIrTYB4cg/w96-h96-n/photo.jpg 2x" class="T75of ZqMJr" aria-hidden="true" data-iml="160194"></div><div class="d15Mdf bAhLNe"><div class="xKpxId zc7KVe"><div class="bAhLNe kx8XBd"><span class="X43Kjb">Miguel Suarez-solis</span><div><span class="nt2C1d"><div class="pf5lIe"><div aria-label="Rated 4 stars out of five stars" role="img"><div class="vQHuPe bUWb7c"></div><div class="vQHuPe bUWb7c"></div><div class="vQHuPe bUWb7c"></div><div class="vQHuPe bUWb7c"></div><div class="L0jl5e bUWb7c"></div></div></div></span><span class="p2TkOb">April 10, 2020</span></div></div><div class="YCMBp GVFJbb"><div jsaction="JIbuQc:isb5Wc(isb5Wc);NrJVc:tUsItb;Juy6d:Hw9KTb;yIJnmd:kuHRr;s4H3C:HBdSge;" jsname="OuHhoc"><div class="XlMhZe"><div role="button" class="U26fgb mUbCce fKz7Od YYBxpf" jslog="77038; 1:1212; track:JIbuQc;" jscontroller="VXdfxd" jsaction="click:cOuCgd; mousedown:UX7yZ; mouseup:lbsD7e; mouseenter:tfO1Yc; mouseleave:JywGue; focus:AHmuwe; blur:O22p3e; contextmenu:mg9Pef;touchstart:p6p2H; touchmove:FwuNnf; touchend:yfqBxc(preventMouseEvents=true|preventDefault=true); touchcancel:JMtRjd;" jsshadow="" jsname="isb5Wc" aria-label="Helpful" aria-disabled="false" tabindex="0" data-tooltip="Helpful" data-tooltip-vertical-offset="-12" data-tooltip-horizontal-offset="0"><div class="VTBa7b MbhUzd" jsname="ksKsZd"></div><span jsslot="" class="xjKiLb"><span class="Ce1Y1c" style="top: -12px"><span class="DPvwYc y92BAb" aria