emove the wall of one of them. It would be nice if I could just put in a really big door ope...<div class="cQj82c"><button class="LkLjZd ScJHi OzU4dc  " jsaction="click:TiglPc" jsname="gxjVle">Full Review</button></div></span><span jsname="fbQN7e" style="display: none;">I like the app overall but does take some playing around with and tricking it to do what I want - such as if I want to have a wall only be half way across a room I have to create two rooms side by side then remove the wall of one of them. It would be nice if I could just put in a really big door opening (without an actual door) in the wall, it would save time. I would also like to be able to create a wall by itself or two walls connected as an L or T without it trying to create an entire room. Sometimes I just want to creatively think through what I'm trying to do. Beyond those suggestions, I am very impressed with the app, far superior to others I've tried. I like the way I can quickly create a room, and the controls are simple to use.</span></div><div class="LVQB0b"><div class="QoPmEb"></div><div><span class="X43Kjb">Marcin Lewandowski</span><span class="p2TkOb">September 22, 2018</span></div>Thank you for the review. There is actually opening symbol under "Doors &amp; Windows". You can change its appearance by clicking "Pattern" icon to remove lines between rooms. To create walls use "Walls" icon. You can drag individual walls from the toolbar or click it and sketch a new room or walls inside a room.</div></div></div></div><div jscontroller="H6eOGe" jsmodel="y8Aajc" jsdata="yf3HXc;gp:AOqpTOFkGxCO3rzI8kSB0JQXPzFEe46Ju6RCMJf1euYv9rGGWdKtjrRCsatUOlgNopeoqBDtigfsJ73cva2L_g;$904 YjFXEf;_;$256"><div class="zc7KVe"><div class="vDSMeb bAhLNe" aria-hidden="true"><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/AOh14Ggap3rB3CaSxeNSdcuF_Bd7OdR8Q7GuM4C1wpK7uQ=w48-h48-n" srcset="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/AOh14Ggap3rB3CaSxeNSdcuF_Bd7OdR8Q7GuM4C1wpK7uQ=w96-h96-n 2x" class="T75of ZqMJr" aria-hidden="true